  "Question": "How many terms are in the arithmetic sequence \\(13,\\) \\(16,\\) \\(19,\\) \\(\\dotsc,\\) \\(70,\\) \\(73?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(20\\)",
    "B": "\\(21\\)",
    "C": "\\(24\\)",
    "D": "\\(60\\)",
    "E": "\\(61\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Consecutive terms differ by \\(3\\), so count how many \\(3\\)-unit steps take us from \\(13\\) to \\(73\\). The total increase is \\(73-13=60\\), giving\n\\[\n\\frac{60}{3}=20\n\\]\ngaps. There is one starting term, and each gap leads to one additional term. Therefore the sequence has \\(20+1=\\boxed{21}\\) terms, choice B.",
